Introduction 
 The ABAP RESTful Application Programming Model (RAP) is SAP's modern programming model for developing business applications and APIs. 
 In RAP, we commonly work with two implementation approaches: 

 Managed RAP: The RAP framework handles most of the transactional processing and database operations. 

 Unmanaged RAP: The developer implements the transactional processing and database operations. 
 But what happens when we want to use the benefits of Managed RAP while still using an existing BAPI or Function Module to save data? 
 This is where Managed RAP with Unmanaged Save becomes useful. 
 In this blog, we will create a simple Sales Header application using RAP and call a custom BAPI during the save process. 
 Comparison of RAP Implementation Types 
 Feature Managed RAP Managed RAP with Unmanaged Save Unmanaged RAP 

